# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
# The first line is 72 characters or fewer, in the imperative mood
# ("add", not "added"), lowercase, with no full stop at the end.
#
# Then a blank line, then the why: the failure that motivated this, or
# the approach you rejected. Wrap at 72 columns. Delete it if the
# change genuinely speaks for itself.
#
# Then a blank line, then footers if there are any:
#   Refs: #12          Closes: #12          Co-Authored-By: Name <email>
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks, and what a caller has to change>
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# type     feat      a new capability
#          fix       behaviour that was wrong, corrected
#          perf      same behaviour, lower cost
#          refactor  same behaviour, different shape
#          docs      documentation only
#          style     formatting only
#          test      tests and verification scripts only
#          build     the build, packaging, or a dependency bump
#          ci        workflows and .github/
#          chore     housekeeping that fits nothing above
#          revert    undoes an earlier commit
#
# scope    content, design, charts, countdown, seo, assets, a11y, docs,
#          deps, ci
#          (optional — leave it off if the change spans the repo)
#
# break    feat(api)!: <description>   plus a BREAKING CHANGE: footer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The whole convention, with examples: CONTRIBUTING.md
# https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
